  situations: [{"t": "Asks the same question again and again","why": ["They can’t hold on to what was just said — it isn’t on purpose","Something is worrying them","Bored or wanting company"],"try": ["Answer again, in the same calm voice","Write the answer on a large note or in their schedule on the home screen","Respond to the feeling: “Are you worried about going out? I’ll be with you.”","Switch to something they enjoy: the story book, a cup of tea"],"avoid": ["Saying “I just told you”","Sighing or looking impatient"]},{"t": "At home but keeps saying “I want to go home”","why": ["“Home” often means feeling safe, a familiar past","More common in the evening, when tired or when it’s noisy","It may signal discomfort or needing the bathroom"],"try": ["Acknowledge the feeling: “You miss home. Tell me about it.”","Look at the story book or old photos together","Take a short walk, offer a drink, check about the bathroom","In the evening, turn up the lights and turn down the TV"],"avoid": ["Arguing “This IS your home”","Locking doors on them or raising your voice"]},{"t": "Restless or upset in the late afternoon","why": ["Tired after the day","Fading light makes things hard to see and scary","Disrupted routine, long daytime naps"],"try": ["Turn on lights and close curtains before dusk","Plan calm afternoon activities: folding laundry, favorite old songs","Get daylight and a walk earlier in the day; keep naps short","Avoid coffee or tea later in the day"],"avoid": ["Scheduling baths or outings in the evening","Reasoning with them or rushing them"]},{"t": "Refuses to bathe","why": ["Cold, afraid of slipping, embarrassed","Can’t follow the steps and feels forced","Bathroom too bright, noisy, or the water feels wrong"],"try": ["Warm the bathroom and lay out towels and clothes first","Offer a foot soak or a warm washcloth instead of “a bath”","Pick a time of day when they’re in a good mood; do a little at a time","Use a towel to cover them and protect their dignity"],"avoid": ["Forcing it or saying they smell","Insisting it must be every day or right now"]},{"t": "Says someone stole their things","why": ["They forgot where they put it and are looking for an explanation","Feeling anxious and losing control"],"try": ["“That’s upsetting. Let’s look for it together.”","When it turns up, don’t point out they misplaced it","Keep a spare of often-lost items (glasses, wallet)","Note their usual hiding spots"],"avoid": ["“You must have lost it yourself”","Arguing about who took it"]},{"t": "Awake at night, days and nights mixed up","why": ["Too little activity or too much napping during the day","Needing the bathroom, pain or discomfort at night","Side effects of medicines"],"try": ["Same wake-up time every morning, with daylight and something to do","A steady bedtime routine: wash up, the same song","Night lights along the way to the bathroom","Fewer drinks, no coffee or tea before bed","If it lasts several days, talk to their doctor"],"avoid": ["Giving sleeping pills on your own","Loudly ordering them back to bed at night"]}],

